    "blurb": "Integrate Camunda with content management systems",
    "overview": "Manage folders and documents in a CMIS-compliant content management system from Camunda-based business processes.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Connect Camunda processes to CMIS-compliant content management systems",
    "splashDescription": "Use this connector to execute operations on a repository that uses the Content Management Interoperability Services (CMIS) standard, which enables different content management systems to communicate over the internet. This protocol is supported by products such as Alfresco and Documentum to store and manage documents. The connector can create and delete folders and upload, download, and delete documents.",
